### 1. The Daily SWIFT Cross-Border Volume

As of 2026, SWIFT processes an average of approximately **45 million to 50 million financial messages per day**. While SWIFT itself is a messaging network and does not hold funds, the underlying monetary value of the transactions cleared via these messages is estimated at roughly **$5 Trillion to $7 Trillion USD daily** in cross-border settlements alone.

When macroeconomists look at onboarding this volume onto a digital ledger, they look at the *annualized liquidity requirements*. A daily volume of $5 Trillion USD translates to an unmeasurable **$1,825 Trillion ($1.825 Quadrillion) USD per year**.

